@echo off
setlocal EnableExtensions
title Capri on XyberRP Staging: her brain, her own voice, Mass Override for everyone
rem ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
rem   Two things only one PC had, for every player on XyberRP Staging:
rem   HER OWN VOICE.  A PC speaks with her real voice only when it installed her local engine
rem   (about 900 MB); every other PC borrowed a Windows voice.  Her same engine and voice files
rem   now run on the game servers' machine, and every player's Capri Voz uses them on launch.  A
rem   PC with her local engine keeps using it; a player's own voice choice stays.
rem   MASS OVERRIDE FOR EVERYONE.  A cast showed on the caster's screen only: the other games never
rem   heard of it.  Now every game follows the gate from its start, and runs every cast near it --
rem   the street around the caster, and the city's lights and billboards for everyone.
rem   AND FROM EVERY PC (2026-11-12): typed as "mass over ride", the brain did not understand it
rem   and nothing happened; and a cast from a PC whose connection drops now and then got lost on its
rem   way to the server, so it ran on that screen only.  Now the brain hears it however it is
rem   typed, and a cast is sent again until the server has it.
rem   LEAVE STAGING FIRST: the package change refuses while anybody is on it.
rem   1. Her voice on the machine, once for the whole machine (nothing when it is there): Pocket TTS
rem      with her voice files from Staging's own package, a test line in English and Spanish, its
rem      own service, and its own private address in the web server with a limit per address --
rem      the web server is checked and put back by itself on any failure.  Then one line in each
rem      language from this PC, the way a player's Capri Voz asks it.  The first time takes a few
rem      minutes (about 1.5 GB is downloaded on the machine).
rem   2. The brain on the machine hears Mass Override however V types it ("mass over ride"): its
rem      program updated, kept first, checked by node, restarted (a second or two: a line Capri thinks
rem      right then may fail), asked; put back by itself on any failure.  Once for the machine.
rem   3. Staging's Mass Override gate updated (it keeps working for older builds), asked from here.
rem   4. The new Capri package: the live one with the brain wired in, Mass Override for every
rem      player, and Capri Voz speaking with her voice from the server -- checked with YOUR GAME'S
rem      OWN Redscript compiler and PowerShell's own parser on this PC; nothing is sent unless both
rem      pass.  Then it goes into Staging's mod store and server.jsonc names it (kept first).
rem   5. The brain's per-address limits (once for the machine; nothing when they are there).
rem   6. Staging restarted: players get the new Capri from the launcher when they join.
rem   7. READ ONLY: what Staging hands out now, checked end to end, her voice asked again.
rem   Nothing else changes: XyberRP's package and the other mods stay as they are.
rem   Logs: kit\capri-*.log here, and ..\open77-av-kit\avkit-restart-*.log.
rem ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
set "PY=%LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\fivem2open77\runtime\python\python.exe"
if not exist "%PY%" goto nopython
set "CK=%~dp0kit\capri_kit.py"
if not exist "%CK%" goto nokit
set "AVK="
if exist "%~dp0..\open77-av-kit\av_kit.py" set "AVK=%~dp0..\open77-av-kit"
if not defined AVK if exist "%USERPROFILE%\Downloads\open77-av-kit\av_kit.py" set "AVK=%USERPROFILE%\Downloads\open77-av-kit"
if not defined AVK goto noavkit
set "AV=%AVK%\av_kit.py"
set "O77_AV_KIT=%AVK%"
@@HOST@@

echo.
echo Next: her own voice and Mass Override for everyone on XyberRP Staging.  Leave Staging
echo first (quit to the menu): the package change refuses while anybody is on it.
choice /C YN /M "Do it on Staging now"
if errorlevel 2 goto declined
echo.
set "RG=0"
echo === 1. Her own voice on the game servers' machine (the first time takes a few minutes)
"%PY%" -X utf8 "%CK%" voice --role staging %HOST%
set "RVO=%ERRORLEVEL%"
if not "%RVO%"=="0" goto novoice
echo.
echo === 2. The brain hears Mass Override however V types it (once for the machine)
"%PY%" -X utf8 "%CK%" brain %HOST%
set "RBR=%ERRORLEVEL%"
if not "%RBR%"=="0" goto nobrain
echo.
echo === 3. Staging's Mass Override gate: every game gets every cast
"%PY%" -X utf8 "%CK%" gate --role staging %HOST%
set "RGA=%ERRORLEVEL%"
if not "%RGA%"=="0" goto nogate
echo.
echo === 4. The new Capri for Staging: built, checked with your game's Redscript, put on Staging
"%PY%" -X utf8 "%CK%" publish --role staging %HOST%
set "RC=%ERRORLEVEL%"
if "%RC%"=="5" goto already
if not "%RC%"=="0" goto notpublished
call :guard
echo.
echo === 6. Staging restarted: players get the new Capri when they join
"%PY%" -X utf8 "%AV%" restart --on open77-xbuniverse-staging %HOST%
set "RS=%ERRORLEVEL%"
if not "%RS%"=="0" goto notrestarted
:verify
echo.
echo === 7. READ ONLY: what Staging hands out now
"%PY%" -X utf8 "%CK%" verify --role staging %HOST%
set "RV=%ERRORLEVEL%"
if not "%RV%"=="0" goto notverified
if not "%RG%"=="0" echo (Step 5 did NOT add the brain's per-address limits: see its lines above.)
echo.
echo Done.  Now on BOTH PCs (the laptop and the desktop):
echo   1. join XyberRP Staging through the Open77 launcher: it names Capri's new build and asks
echo      once before installing it (it carries a DLL) -- accept;
echo   2. load in: on the desktop her greeting should NOT mention a Windows voice, and she speaks
echo      with her own voice (it comes from the server: the first line can take a second or two);
echo   3. stand near each other and type Mass Override to Capri on one PC, the way you do ("mass
echo      over ride" works now): the other PC's street, lights and billboards should go too, within
echo      a few seconds -- then the same from the other PC;
echo   4. then run C1 here: it shows her voice's last lines and every game the gate saw run a cast.
echo Then tell Claude how it went.  If all is fine, C3 does the same for live XyberRP.
pause
exit /b 0

:already
echo.
echo Staging's Capri package already has all of this: nothing changed in it.
call :guard
goto verify

:guard
echo.
echo === 5. The brain's per-address limits (its private address goes to every player)
"%PY%" -X utf8 "%CK%" guard %HOST%
set "RG=%ERRORLEVEL%"
exit /b 0

:declined
echo.
echo Nothing done, nothing changed.
pause
exit /b 0

:novoice
echo.
echo Her voice is NOT on the machine (exit %RVO%): see the lines above, and tell Claude "done".
echo Nothing else was changed: the gate and Staging's Capri package are as they were.
pause
exit /b %RVO%

:nobrain
echo.
echo The brain was NOT updated (exit %RBR%): see the lines above, and tell Claude "done".  It is as
echo it was (put back by itself if anything failed).  Nothing else was changed.
pause
exit /b %RBR%

:nogate
echo.
echo Staging's Mass Override gate was NOT updated, or it does not answer (exit %RGA%): the old
echo gate is back if anything failed.  Staging's Capri package was not changed.  Tell Claude "done".
pause
exit /b %RGA%

:notpublished
echo.
echo Staging's Capri was NOT changed (exit %RC%): see the lines above, and tell Claude "done".
echo (exit 3: somebody is on Staging -- you too count -- or its Capri changed meanwhile: leave
echo it and run this again.  exit 2: this PC could not check the package with your game's
echo Redscript -- the lines above say why.  exit 1: something else; nothing was sent.)
echo Her voice, the brain and the gate (steps 1-3) are in place and harmless without the new package.
pause
exit /b %RC%

:notrestarted
echo.
echo Staging's server.jsonc names the new Capri, but Staging did not restart (exit %RS%).  exit 3:
echo somebody joined meanwhile -- leave it and run this again (the change is in, the restart is
echo what is missing).  exit 4: the Open77 master server refused the start for now: Staging is
echo stopped, run this again in a few minutes.  Tell Claude "done".
pause
exit /b %RS%

:notverified
echo.
echo Staging restarted, but what it hands out is not checked yet (exit %RV%): see the lines above
echo and tell Claude "done".  C2b puts Staging's Capri back.
pause
exit /b %RV%

:nopython
echo FAILED: fivem2open77 Studio's Python is not at %PY% - is the Studio installed?
pause
exit /b 1

:nokit
echo FAILED: this folder's own kit (kit\capri_kit.py) is missing: unpack the whole folder again.
pause
exit /b 1

:noavkit
echo FAILED: the AV kit's av_kit.py was not found: not in %~dp0..\open77-av-kit, not in
echo %USERPROFILE%\Downloads\open77-av-kit.  It signs in to the machine the way the Studio does.
pause
exit /b 1
